EWS_TRAINING_SPEC_TEXT: str = """
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
SAT-GUARD EWS v3.0  —  PRODUCTION TRAINING SPECIFICATION
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

DATASET
───────
Name:         UK-DNO-Grid-Weather-2018-2024
Sources:      Northern Powergrid SCADA / IMS (incident data)
              Open-Meteo ERA5 Reanalysis (15-min, 0.25° grid)
              Environment Agency River Gauge Network
              UK-AIR AURN Network (air quality)
              Met Office MIDAS surface observations
              NESO (formerly ESO) generation mix API
              Ofgem DNO Incident Database
Period:       2018-01-01 to 2024-06-30
Resolution:   15-minute
n_samples:    ~230,400  (6.5 years × 365.25 × 96 steps/day)
n_features:   72
n_targets:    5  (risk_score, grid_fail_prob, ENS_mw, exceedance_p, loss_£m)
Train/Val/Test: 70% / 15% / 15% (stratified by storm severity quintile × season)
Missing data: Forward-fill ≤3 steps; linear interpolation ≤12 steps; drop otherwise
Outlier treatment: IQR winsorisation at [1%, 99%] per feature
Augmentation: MixUp α=0.2 on training set
              Synthetic storm sequences via conditional WaveNet GAN
              (50,000 additional sequences; peak risk >60 oversampled 3×)

ARCHITECTURE TRAINING REGIMES
──────────────────────────────

BiLSTM + Attention
  Input shape:    (batch, 48, 72)  — 48 × 15-min steps = 12h history
  Architecture:   Embedding(72→64) → BiLSTM(128, 2L) → Dropout(0.25)
                  → Temporal Self-Attention(d=128) → Dense(64,gelu) → Dense(3)
  Loss:           Pinball(τ=[0.10,0.50,0.90]) + 0.30 × MSE
  Optimiser:      AdamW lr=3e-4, weight_decay=1e-5
  Scheduler:      CosineAnnealingWarmRestarts(T0=30, η_min=1e-6)
  Epochs:         150   Early stopping patience=15 monitor=val_CRPS
  Batch size:     256
  Parameters:     ~4.1M
  Training time:  ~6h on A100 GPU

Temporal Fusion Transformer (TFT)
  Input shape:    Static(5) + Known future(6,96) + Unknown past(61,96)
  Architecture:   Variable selection networks → GRN → Multi-head attention(8,128)
                  → Point-wise FFN + GLU → Quantile output heads
  Loss:           Pinball(τ=[0.10,0.50,0.90]) + Symmetric MAPE × 0.15
  Optimiser:      AdamW lr=1e-4, warmup=1000 steps, cosine decay
  Epochs:         200   Early stopping patience=20 monitor=val_CRPS
  Batch size:     128
  Parameters:     ~12.2M
  Training time:  ~18h on A100 GPU
  Note:           Best overall model. CRPS 0.26.

WaveNet Dilated Causal CNN
  Input shape:    (batch, 255, 72)  — 255 × 15-min steps = ~63h history
  Architecture:   8 dilated causal conv layers, rates=[1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128]
                  Gated activation: tanh(Wf*x) ⊙ σ(Wg*x)
                  Skip + residual connections → 1×1 conv → quantile output
  Loss:           Pinball(τ=[0.10,0.50,0.90])
  Optimiser:      Adam lr=2e-4
  Epochs:         120
  Batch size:     512 (parallelisable — fastest training)
  Parameters:     ~2.8M
  Training time:  ~3h on A100 GPU
  Note:           Fastest inference (2.1ms). Best T+5min model.

CNN-BiLSTM Hybrid
  Architecture:   Branch A: Conv1D(64,k=5,relu)→MaxPool(2)→Conv1D(128,k=3,relu)→MaxPool(2)
                  Branch B: BiLSTM(96) → Dropout(0.30)
                  Merge: Concat → Dense(128,gelu) → Dense(3)
  Loss:           Pinball(τ=[0.10,0.50,0.90]) + MSE × 0.20
  Optimiser:      Adam lr=2e-4
  Epochs:         130   Batch: 256   Parameters: ~3.3M
  Training time:  ~5h on A100 GPU

Latent Neural ODE
  Architecture:   Encoder: GRU(64) → μ₀, σ₀ (variational)
                  ODE func: MLP(3L, 64 hidden, tanh) integrated via Dormand-Prince RK45
                  Decoder: MLP(2L) → risk distribution (μ, σ)
  Loss:           ELBO = Reconstruction loss + β × KL divergence
  Optimiser:      Adam lr=1e-3 → 1e-4 (warmup 500 steps)
  Epochs:         150   Batch: 64 (ODE solver overhead)   Parameters: ~5.6M
  Training time:  ~22h on A100 GPU (ODE solver dominates)
  Note:           Handles irregular observation gaps. Most theoretically principled.

Stacked GRU + Skip Connections
  Architecture:   GRU(96) → GRU(128) → GRU(64), all with skip connections
                  Output: Σ(skip_i × w_i) × horizon-aware weights
  Loss:           Pinball(τ=[0.10,0.50,0.90])
  Optimiser:      AdamW lr=3e-4
  Epochs:         120   Batch: 256   Parameters: ~2.1M
  Training time:  ~3.5h on A100 GPU

N-BEATS Probabilistic
  Architecture:   3 stacks × 4 blocks:
                  Stack 1: Polynomial basis [1,t,t²,t³] (trend)
                  Stack 2: Fourier basis (K=12 harmonics) (seasonality)
                  Stack 3: MLP residual (generic)
                  Each block: (backcast, forecast) doubly residual
  Loss:           NLL under learned output distribution
  Optimiser:      Adam lr=1e-3
  Epochs:         100   Batch: 512   Parameters: ~1.9M
  Training time:  ~2.5h on A100 GPU

Extended Kalman Filter (no training required)
  Process noise Q: diag([4.0, 1.0, 0.5, 0.002])  — hand-tuned
  Observation noise R: diag([9.0, 2.5, 1.5, 0.005]) — hand-tuned
  Initial state covariance P₀: diag([25, 4, 1, 0.01])
  Calibration: Minimise RMSE on validation set via Nelder-Mead (10 parameters)
  Note: No GPU required. Sub-ms inference. Pure physics prior.

XGBoost (no GPU required)
  n_estimators=100, max_depth=6, learning_rate=0.10
  subsample=0.80, colsample_bytree=0.80
  objective=reg:quantileerror + tweedie variance
  Early stopping: 15 rounds on val set
  Training time: ~2 min on 8-core CPU

LEVEL-2 META-LEARNER (Stacked Generalisation)
  Input:   Concatenated L1 q50 outputs (9-dim)
  Output:  Final q10, q50, q90
  Model:   Ridge regression (α=0.1) — sklearn
  Fitting: 5-fold cross-validation on training set (out-of-fold predictions)
  Update:  Retrained when any L1 model is updated

ENSEMBLE POST-PROCESSING
  Temperature scaling: T calibrated on validation set (T=1.15, grid search)
  Conformal correction: Coverage factor derived from validation residuals
  CRPS calibration:    Model weights updated quarterly via coordinate descent

RETRAINING SCHEDULE
  L1 models:   Quarterly full retraining (new 3-month data batch)
  Meta-learner: Monthly refit
  CRPS weights: Monthly recalibration
  Kalman Q,R:   Monthly recalibration via Nelder-Mead
  KPI trigger:  Retrain immediately if rolling 30-day CRPS degrades > 0.05

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
"""


